cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  shmap-rs: a Rust port of shmap, with a reproducible
  cross-architecture benchmark suite
message: >-
  If you use this software or its benchmark result sets,
  please cite it using the metadata below. The algorithm is
  Ivanov et al.'s; please cite the original shmap as well.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Panchev
    given-names: Dobromir
    email: dobromir.panchev@gmail.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0000-2636-2593'
  - family-names: Ivanov
    given-names: Pesho
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8119-3849'
repository-code: https://github.com/d0bromir/shmap-rs
license: MPL-2.0
version: 1.4.1
abstract: >-
  A Rust port of shmap, a sketch-based long-read mapper that
  locates a read by k-mer set overlap rather than by
  alignment. Mapping decisions match the C++ original; the
  port is faster single-threaded, uses substantially less
  memory, and adds threading.

  The repository also carries the evidence: a versioned
  benchmark suite whose every published figure is generated
  from a committed result set and checked against it, run on
  both x86_64 and aarch64, with concordance scored against
  Winnowmap2 and every counter reproduced exactly across the
  two architectures.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - sequence alignment
  - long-read mapping
  - minimizers
  - sketching
  - reproducible benchmarking
  - rust
references:
  - type: software
    title: shmap
    repository-code: https://github.com/pesho-ivanov/shmap
    license: MPL-2.0
